endent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "84ef027b485585402e596eb8eb63de796408e56df0812e5f2a2a126638a903d0", "hash": "b0e63f6d60013e40ea705c9c10c92e9b8fadb0aa5a916da1c91b00acc438fa56"}, {"seq": 2325, "time": "2026-10-28T13:38:08.249135+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 45893, "provider_input_hash": "76655f5dcef94157895339b79c1e28f84eb3933938239195d013f189d1449f7b", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-8fe345439d9b479e"}, "prev_hash": "b0e63f6d60013e40ea705c9c10c92e9b8fadb0aa5a916da1c91b00acc438fa56", "hash": "3f0aaf4ad2088ebe6701210c289089b6693f36417ef92a491f796d0ed534884f"}, {"seq": 2326, "time": "2026-10-28T13:38:48.233546+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 45893, "provider_input_hash": "76655f5dcef94157895339b79c1e28f84eb3933938239195d013f189d1449f7b", "result": "daily_quota", "retry_after_seconds": 62175.83738875389}, "id": "w-8fe345439d9b479e"}, "prev_hash": "3f0aaf4ad2088ebe6701210c289089b6693f36417ef92a491f7